<Doc
  title="Forwarding"
  description="Copy every stored span on to another OTLP endpoint, so mcpd is one hop in a telemetry pipeline rather than a place data goes to be trapped. Local storage always happens first."
  lede="mcpd speaks OTLP in both directions. Nothing that arrives is stuck here."
  og="docs"
>
  <h2>One protocol out, not eleven exporters</h2>
  <p>
    mcpd receives OTLP, and it can emit OTLP. That single property replaces most
    of what a set of per-vendor exporters does: Langfuse, Datadog, Honeycomb,
    Grafana, and every other destination worth naming accept OTLP over HTTP.
    Forwarding is therefore one implementation rather than eleven, and it cannot
    fall behind a vendor's SDK release.
  </p>
  <p>
    It also means adopting mcpd is reversible. Point it at whatever you were
    using before, run both for a fortnight, and decide with the data in front of
    you rather than on a migration you cannot undo.
  </p>

  <h2>Turning it on</h2>

  <Command
    class="not-prose my-6"
    title="store locally and copy onward"
    command="mcpd serve --forward-endpoint https://otlp.example.com"
  />

  <p>
    The path is appended, so give the base URL and not
    <code>/v1/traces</code>. For a destination that needs credentials, add
    headers:
  </p>

  <Command
    class="not-prose my-6"
    title="with an authorization header"
    command={`mcpd serve \\
  --forward-endpoint https://otlp.example.com \\
  --forward-header 'Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN'`}
  />

  <p>
    The same settings live under <code>forward</code> in the config file, where
    <code>batch_size</code> and <code>enabled</code> are also available. A flag
    beats the file, so one instance can be pointed elsewhere without editing a
    shared ConfigMap.
  </p>

  <pre><code class="language-json">{`{
  "forward": {
    "endpoint": "https://otlp.example.com",
    "headers": [["Authorization", "Bearer sk-..."]],
    "batch_size": 256,
    "enabled": true
  }
}`}</code></pre>

  {/* The diagram belongs here, not at the top. It draws the intake ending at
      Store, and this section is about what happens after Store, so the two read
      as one sequence rather than as a picture that stops where the subject
